From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:54:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: honour FEX_HOSTFEATURES' LRCPC2 switch on the iOS
 host

The iOS branch of CPUFeatures::FetchHostFeatures builds the feature set
by hand and returns before FEX::FetchHostFeatures, so
SupportsTSOImm9 (FEAT_LRCPC2) is always false there and
enablelrcpc2 in FEX_HOSTFEATURES is read and ignored. With LRCPC2 a
TSO load or store with a small offset is one LDAPUR or STLUR instead
of an address add and an LDAPR or STLR. Code at EL0 cannot read the ID registers on iOS, so the
host app asks the kernel and passes enablelrcpc2; honour that switch,
and disablelrcpc2, the way fex 0005 honours disableafp, and log the
state the JIT uses.

Class: host-app
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-28-fex-memory-ordering.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp
index 460e78044..4cc531314 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp
@@ -87,7 +87,19 @@ FEXCore::HostFeatures CPUFeatures::FetchHostFeatures(bool IsWine, FEXCore::HostF
     if (HostFeatureControl() & FEXCore::Config::HostFeatures::DISABLEAFP) {
       HostFeatures.SupportsAFP = false;
     }
-    LogMan::Msg::IFmt("FEX: iOS host AFP={} (FEX_HOSTFEATURES={})", HostFeatures.SupportsAFP, HostFeatureControl());
+    /* Playport: and its LRCPC2 switch. FEAT_LRCPC2's LDAPUR and STLUR take
+     * a signed 9-bit offset, so a TSO load or store needs no separate
+     * address add. Code at EL0 cannot read the ID registers on iOS, so the
+     * host app asks the kernel (sysctl hw.optional.arm.FEAT_LRCPC2) and
+     * passes the answer as enablelrcpc2; without it this stays off. */
+    if (HostFeatureControl() & FEXCore::Config::HostFeatures::ENABLELRCPC2) {
+      HostFeatures.SupportsTSOImm9 = true;
+    }
+    if (HostFeatureControl() & FEXCore::Config::HostFeatures::DISABLELRCPC2) {
+      HostFeatures.SupportsTSOImm9 = false;
+    }
+    LogMan::Msg::IFmt("FEX: iOS host AFP={} LRCPC2={} (FEX_HOSTFEATURES={})", HostFeatures.SupportsAFP,
+                      HostFeatures.SupportsTSOImm9, HostFeatureControl());
   }
   HostFeatures.CPUMIDRs.push_back(0u);
   HostFeatures.HostType = HostType;
